# What must stay out of the upload to Cloud Build.
#
# `gcloud run deploy --source .` sends this folder to Cloud Build first, and
# Cloud Build then makes the image. This file controls the upload. The
# `.dockerignore` file controls a different step: what the `COPY` lines of the
# Dockerfile put into a layer of the image.
#
# The two files are almost the same, and they differ in one important way.
# `.dockerignore` holds `Dockerfile`, because the image does not need a copy of
# its own recipe. This file must NOT hold `Dockerfile`, because Cloud Build
# reads the Dockerfile to make the image. A `Dockerfile` line here stops the
# deploy.
#
# This folder is not a Git repository. Without this file `gcloud` uploads every
# file, and that includes `.venv/` and `web/node_modules/`. Both hold many
# thousands of files for the wrong platform, so the upload is large and slow and
# it gives the build nothing.
#
# The syntax is the syntax of `.gitignore`.

# Secrets. A file that goes into a layer of an image stays in that layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json
gcp-credentials*.json

# The virtual environment of the development machine. The image makes its own
# with `uv sync`, and this folder holds binary files for the wrong platform.
.venv/
venv/

# The interface. The first stage of the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and
# `npm run build`, so it makes both of these folders itself.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Git history.
.git/
.gitignore

# Python build files and cache folders.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# The tests and the documents. The service does not read them at run time.
#
# `README.md` stays. `pyproject.toml` names it in the `readme` field, and `uv`
# reads that field, so a build with no README can fail there.
tests/
docs/
projectsync_full_spec.md

# Notes of the agent tools. The service does not read them.
.claude/
.adk/
.agents/

# Editors, the operating system, and local run files.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
.firestore-emulator/
scratch/

# Note for a person who edits this file: the `memory/` folder at the top level
# is a Python package that the service imports at run time. It is not a note
# folder. Do not add it here.
